{"id":"word:hebrew:H2803","type":"word","title":"חָשַׁב","subtitle":"H2803 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to plait or interpenetrate , i.e. (literally) to weave or (generally) to fabricate ; figuratively, to plot or contrive (usually in a malicious sense); hence (from the mental effort) to think , regard , value , compute","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָשַׁב (H2803) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 124 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָשַׁב (châshab) means properly, to plait or interpenetrate , i.e. (literally) to weave or (generally) to fabricate ; figuratively, to plot or contrive (usually in a malicious sense); hence (from the mental effort) to think , regard , value , compute First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 10 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָשַׁב","transliteration":"châshab","pronunciation":"khaw-shab'","strong":"H2803","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2803","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["חָשַׁ֖ב","חֹשֵׁ֖ב","חֹשֵׁ֛ב","וְ/חִשַּׁב","נֶחְשָׁ֛ב"],"morphs":[["HVqrmsa",14],["HVqp3ms",8],["HVNi3ms",8],["HVqp3cp",7],["HVNp3cp",7],["HVqi3ms",6],["HC/Vpq3ms",5],["HVNi3fs",4],["HVNrmsa",3],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3fs",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to plait or interpenetrate , i.e. (literally) to weave or (generally) to fabricate ; figuratively, to plot or contrive (usually in a malicious sense); hence (from the mental effort) to think , regard , value , compute","usage":"(make) account (of), conceive, consider, count, cunning (man, work, workman), devise, esteem, find out, forecast, hold, imagine, impute, invent, be like, mean, purpose, reckon(-ing be made), regard, think.","full":"H2803. chashab חָשַׁב verb think, account (Late Hebrew id. ; Aramaic חֲשַׁב , ; Arabic ; Ethiopic id. ; Phoenician noun חשב meaning dubious see CIS i. 86 ) — Qal Perfect ׳ח Isa 33:8-9 t.; חָשַׁבְתָּה 2Sam 14:13 etc.; Imperfect יַחְשֹׁב Isa 10:7 4 t.; יַחֲשָׁבֿ 2Sam 19:20 ; Psalm 40:18; suffix יַחְשְׁבֵנִי Job 19:11 ; 33:10 ; plural יַחְשְׁבוּ Psa 41:8 ; Dan 11:25 ; יַחְשֹׁ֑בוּ Isa 13:17 ; יַחֲשֹׁבוּן Psa 35:20 ; נַחְשְׁבָה Jer 18:18 , etc. + 9 t. Imperfect; Infinitive construct לַחְשֹׁב Exod 31:4 3 t.; Participle חשֵׁב 26:1 15 t., חוֺשֵׁב 2Chr 26:15 ; חשְׁבִים Neh 6:2-3 t., חשְׁבֵי Micah 2:1 3 t.; — I. of man : 1 think , account יחשׁב כן לא לבבו Isa 10:7 not so thinketh his mind ; שׁמוֺ חשׁבי Mal 3:16 those thinking of his name ; followed by 2 accusative נגוע חשׁבנהו Isa 53:4 we thought him stricken ; elsewhere with accusative + לְ Gen 38:15 (J), 1Sam 1:13 ; Job 19:15 ; 35:2 ; 41:24 ; so, figurative, of crocodile 41:19 he reckoneth iron as straw . 2 devise, plan, mean , with accusative רָעָה מַחֲשֶׁבֶת Ezek 38:10 , רעה Psa 35:4 ; 140:3 ; Zech 7:10 ; 8:17 , תַּהְמֻּכ֑וֺת Prov 16:30 , מְזִמּוֺת Psa 10:2 ; 21:12 , מִרְמוֺת דִּבְרֵי 35:20 , אָוֶן Micah 2:1 ; Ezek 11:2 ; Psa 36:5 , הַוּוֺת 52:4 ; ׳ח על רע(ה) devise evil against Gen 50:20 (E), Jer 48:2 ; Nahum 1:11 , ׳ח לְ רעה Psa 41:8 , ׳ח על מַחֲשֶׁבֶת Jer 11:19 ; 18:18 ; 49:30 ; Dan 11:25 ; Est 8:3 ; 9:25 , ׳ח על כזאת 2Sam 14:13 ; with infinitive 1Sam 18:25 ; Jer 18:8 ; 23:27 ; Job 6:26 ; Neh 6:2 , 6 ; Est 9:24 ; Psa 140:5 ; with לבלתי + Imperfect 2Sam 14:14 (where, however, Ew reads חוֺבֵ for וחשׁב compare We Dr; in this case לבלתי carries on יִשָּׂא לֹא ). 3 charge, impute ׳ח ל ׳עון , 2Sam 19:20 impute iniquity to . 4 esteem, value, regard , silver Isa 13:17 , a man 33:8 , the servant of ׳י 53:3 . 5 invent ingenious and artistic things, ׳ח שׁיר כלי להם Amos 6:5 invent for themselves instruments of music; ׳ח מחשׁבת (כל) invent cunning work (of artistic devices in construction of tabernacle) Exod 31:4 ; 35:32 , 35 (all P), so 2Chr 2:13 ; חשֵׁב מַעֲשֵׂה work of the cunning (ingenious, inventive) workman (of artistic devices in weaving; see especially VB and Di) Exod 26:1 , 31 ; 28:6 , 15 ; 36:8 , 35 ; 39:3 , 8 (all P); חוֺשֵׁב מַחֲשֶׁבֶת 2Chr 26:15 inventions of inventive men (of engines of war); וְחשֵׁב חָרָשׁ craftsman and inventive workman (in construction of tabernacle, see above) Exod 35:35 ; 38:23 (P). II. of God : 1 think , with accusative pers + לְ indirect object account one לאויב , for an enemy Job 13:24 ; 33:10 ; ׳ח כצריו לוֺ 19:11 he accounted me unto him as his adversaries . 2 devise, plan, mean , with accusative + ל indirect object לטבה for good Gen 50:20 (E); with ל person לִי devise for me Psalm 40:18; accusative of thing + עַל , devise something against a person Micah 2:3 ; Jer 18:11 ; towards one 29:11 , with אל against 49:20 ; 50:45 ; followed by infinitive 26:3 ; 36:3 ; Lam 2:8 . 3 impute, reckon , with accusative of thing + ל person, the habit of believing in ׳י he reckoned to Abram as righteousness Gen 15:6 (J E; compare Niph`al 3 ); not impute iniquity to one Psa 32:2 . Niph`al Perfect נֶחְשַׁב Num 18:27 , 30 , נֶחְשַׁבְתִּי Psa 88:5 etc. + 10 t. Perfect; Imperfect יֵחָשֵׁב Lev 7:18 7 t., etc., + 6 t. Imperfect; Participle נֶחְשָׁב Isa 2:22 ; 1Kin 10:21 ; 2Chr 9:20 : — 1 be accounted, thought, esteemed , with כְּ as Hosea 8:12 ; Isa 5:28 ; 29:16 ; 40:15 ; Psa 44:23 ; Job 18:3 ; 41:21 ; with לְ Isa 29:17 = 32:15 , Lam 4:2 ; עִם with, among Psa 88:5 , בַּמֶּה Isa 2:22 at what (value) ? (see probably interpolated; omitted by ᵐ5 ); with accusative Deut 2:11 , 20 ; Prov 17:28 ; Neh 13:13 ; לוֺ נֶחְשַׁבְנוּ נָכְרִיּוֺת Gen 31:13 (E; ᵐ5 Sam ׳כְּנֶח ) Isa 40:17 . 2 be computed, reckoned , with לְ Josh 13:3 (D), עַל Lev 25:31 (P), 2Sam 4:2 : absolute כסף was not counted (so plentiful was it) 1Kin 10:21 2Chr 9:20 ; 2Kin 22:7 . 3 be imputed to any one , with לְ Lev 7:18 ; Num 18:27 , 30 (all P), Lev 17:4 (H) Prov 27:14 ; the interposition of Phinehas ׳נח לצדקה לוֺ Psa 106:31 was imputed to him for righteousness (compare Qal II 3 ). Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular חִשַּׁב Lev 25:27 4 t.; feminine חִשְּׁבָה Jonah 1:4 ; 1 singular חִשַּׁבְתִּי Psa 77:6 ; 119:59 ; Imperfect יְחַשֵּׁב Prov 16:9 ; Dan 11:24 , תְּחַשְּׁבוּן Nahum 1:9 , etc., + 4 t. Imperfect; Participle מְחַשֵּׁב Prov 24:8 : &#8212; 1 think upon, consider, be mindful of , with accusative Psa 77:6 ; 119:59 , וַתְּחַשְּׁבֵהוּ בֶּןאֱֿנוֺשׁ (מה) 144:3 what (is) man's son, and thou thinkest upon him (|| תֵּדָעֵהוּ ). 2 think to do, devise, plan , with accusative Prov 16:9 , אֶל of persons against whom Hosea 7:15 ; Nahum 1:9 , עַל Dan 11:24 ; with infinitive Psa 73:16 ; Prov 24:8 ; so of inanimate object לְהִשָּׁבֵר חִשְּׁבָה הָאֳנִיָּה Jonah 1:4 the ship was about to (minded to) be broken up . 3 count, reckon , the years since a sale of land Lev 25:27 (H); with לְ person 25:52 (H), 27:18 , 23 (P); with עִם 25:50 (P); with אֶת 2Kin 12:16 . Hithpa`el Imperfect יִתְחַשָּׁ֑ב לֹא בַּגּוֺיִם Num 23:9 (JE) among the nations it shall not reckon itself . [ חֲשַׁב ] verb think, account (see Biblical Hebrew); — Pe`al Participle pass plural חֲשִׁיבִון כְּלָה Dan 4:32 like those not accounted of , of no account, Bev Dr.","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 10 21","keyReferences":["1Kgs 10 21","1Sam 1 13","1Sam 18 25","2Chr 2 13","2Chr 9 20","2Chr 26 15","2Kgs 12 16","2Kgs 22 7"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":124,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 10 21","book":"1Kgs","chapter":10,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נֶחְשָׁ֛ב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVNrmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 13","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּחְשְׁבֶ֥/הָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 18 25","book":"1Sam","chapter":18,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חָשַׁ֔ב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3ms"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/לַ/חְשֹׁ֖ב","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Vqc"},{"reference":"2Chr 9 20","book":"2Chr","chapter":9,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נֶחְ